# CG Panel / Desk UI

Vocabulary and ownership: see `cg.mdc`.

**Panel layout:** one page, two columns — **Package** (master surface, card bg + soft depth) vs **Layers** (nested workbench, quieter bg). Prefer spacing / surface over hairline borders. Header: Back + Package + Alpha/Dim + Copy OBS; Layers header: Layers + Alpha/Dim + catalog. Then monitor section, Name / Role / Appear / Look, footer Delete package (`mat-flat-button.danger-btn`). Right: tiles then selected Layer desk as one inset card (settings | visual). Desk footer: Delete layer + Copy layer OBS. Click selected tile again to close desk. Package title is heavier than Layers.

## Edit mode (per package, localStorage `cg-package-edit-mode:{id}`)
| Mode | Monitors | Package mix | Take |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Studio mode** ON (default) | Pending \| On air on Package column | Waits for **Take**: name, role, Appear, Package Look, Layer existence / On-Off / z-order | Required |
| **Studio mode** OFF (= Direct) | One On air monitor | Auto-saves (debounced ~450ms) + Realtime broadcast | Hidden once package exists (first **Create** still needed); turning Studio off while dirty promotes immediately |

Layer content is never gated by Package Take (see Ownership in `cg.mdc`). Hide-mid-edit workflow: Package Off → Take → edit Layer → On → Take. Skipping Take after Off can still hit OBS while visible — accepted risk.

## Layer desk has no Studio mode
Layer content (Logo and Subtitle) is always Live: edits write through to DB, then publish to OBS (debounced ~450ms). When `CgService.onAirOutput` really lists the layer, the desk shows "This layer is on air. Edits go to OBS now." (reserved 28px row above the monitor).

## On air / Pending
- Studio: two 16:9 Stages — **Pending left** (`CgMixPreview`, draft), **On air right** (`CgProgram`, same data as OBS). New unsaved Package: On air empty.
- Direct: one On air Stage (`CgProgram`, not the draft).
- Layer tiles use `CgMixPreview` (`wide`, `forceVisible`, Package pending Look) — same component as the desk monitor.
- Live cue (Up / Down / Blank / Paste / Load) and Cue Fade / Cut always update On air immediately in both modes. Alpha / Dim toggles sit next to **Package** and **Layers** — no Backdrop label.

## Controls & heights (Panel & Desk)
- `.cg-seg-btn`, `.cg-seg-toggle`, `input`, `select`: uniform **28px** outer height, `box-sizing: border-box`.
- Inputs/selects: 1px border. Toggle groups: `height: 28px`, inner buttons `26px`.
- `.cg-seg-btn`: `height/min-height/max-height/line-height: 28px` (overrides Aero 32px).
- `.cg-monitor-toolbar` locked to 28px (`flex-shrink: 0; overflow: hidden`) so preview position is stable with or without Apply / Discard.

## Mouse wheel (every number input and dropdown)
Hover is enough (no focus needed); the field swallows the wheel. Directives `appCgWheel` (number `input`) and `appCgWheelSelect` (`select`) live in `core/domains/cg/cg-wheel.directive.ts`; they read the ngModel value and emit the next one (`appCgWheelChange`), the component writes the model the same way typing does. Up = increase; dropdown down = next option, stops at both ends. Alt = fine (step ÷10), Shift = coarse (×10; Windows moves the delta to `deltaX`). Off-grid values snap to the grid first (0.104 → 0.11). Clamped to `min` / `max`; an unchanged value emits nothing. Layer content is Live, so wheel edits go to OBS like typing (450ms debounce); no lock when on air.
- Steps: X / Y 0.1, Scale 0.05, ms 50 (fine 10, coarse 500; wheel floor `CG_WHEEL_MIN_FADE_MS` so it never turns into Cut), Size (vh) 0.1, 字距 0.01, 行距 0.05, Scale X / Y 0.05, Stroke 0.01, Shadow Angle 15 (fine 1, coarse 45, wraps 360 → 0), Shadow Distance / Radius 0.5, Gradient Angle 15 (same wrap as Shadow Angle).
- Font wheel skips "Other…". Cue ms writes are debounced and coalesced in `CgService.patchLayerTransition` (draft updates at once).

## Always desktop (Panel only)
`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…` lock viewport `width=1280`, `min-width: 1280px`. No stacked `@media` reflow. **List** is responsive. Overlay `/o` and `/cg-live` stay `width=device-width`. Unlock when leaving Panel.

## Theme and buttons
- No fixed CG palette; follow the operator's Aero/Material + light/dark. Do not recreate `_cg-theme.scss`.
- Real Angular Material only, not hand-rolled `.cg-btn`:
  - Either-choice groups (Channel/Source, Fade/Cut, Color/B&W, Alpha/Dim, News/Show, Cue Fade/Cut): `mat-button-toggle-group.cg-seg-toggle`.
  - One-shot actions (Delete / Copy OBS `content_copy` / Choose local image / catalog / cue / Copy): `mat-stroked-button.cg-seg-btn`.
  - Only **Create** / **Take** / Logo **Apply**: `mat-flat-button` primary.
  - Destructive: `mat-flat-button.danger-btn`.
  - **Studio mode** is a labeled `.cg-switch` in the Package monitor toolbar only. Layer On/Off is `.cg-switch`.
  - Back is plain circular `<a class="cg-back">`. Package Copy OBS sits right after Package Alpha/Dim; Layers catalog is `margin-left: auto`.
- Sentence case labels; no uppercase transform.

## No global toolbar
`<app-toolbar>` hidden for Panel paths via `isCgPanelPath()`. **List** (`/cg`, `/cg/list`) uses the normal AppToolbar through `HeaderService` (title, back to Welcome, Refresh, New package). Panel keeps Back / Studio mode / Take inline.

## Layer desk
- Single preview for that one Layer, own local Alpha/Dim backdrop. Desk Look is **Layer Look only** (`layerLookOnly`); Package B&W does not grey the desk. Desk force-shows the layer even when Package Off (`forceVisible`). Desk does not bind Package Appear duration.
- Tiles: chrome on top (`drag_indicator` + z + On/Off), Stage thumb, **name** at bottom (custom `name`, or Element type if blank).
- Desk left: live-on-air warning row + Stage ~450px + **Name | Look** side by side + **Source** (Logo / Subtitle load-paste) + footer one row: Copy to package + Delete layer + Copy layer OBS. Right: **Place** (Anchor / X / Y / Scale + Outline switch) for Logo. Subtitle right is two columns (Cue+queue | Place+Style) when the desk is ≥1300px (`@container`); narrower stacks and scrolls. Place numbers use fixed width. No Inherit / Follow package option. Tiles (`.cg-drive`) shrink while a desk is open.
- Greyscale is a per-layer host `filter` and always cuts. Package Appear only drives host opacity. Must not change z-order.

## Logo / Subtitle desk details
- Logo Anchor: 3x3 directional button grid (`cg-anchor-toggle-group`, arrow icons, dark blue when selected); X / Y / Scale inputs (no Unit / Width controls). X / Y labels say which edge they measure from (`From right`, `From top`); on a centered axis the input is a greyed `—` and the value is ignored (value kept in data). Desk **Outline** toggle (not saved, not OBS): thick yellow rim + red outer shadow.
- Subtitle desk: column A = monitor + Source + footer; column B = Cue (Up / Down / Blank / Fade-Cut, then ms) + filling queue; column C = Place (Anchor 3x3 + **Align** left / center / right icon toggle under it + X/Y/Scale (no Width); same ignored-axis `—` behaviour as Logo) then Style (no text-align control there). Empty Logo-only toolbar is hidden. Clock and Weather desk (right column): Background (optional image, Logo-style Source + Place + Outline + Clear), Text place (Anchor, Align, X / Y), Style (`cg-text-style-editor`), then Clock (format, language, timezone, Live/Custom, datetime + Push) or Weather (place search, unit mode). Background and text are placed separately.
- Cue bar icons: `keyboard_arrow_up` / `keyboard_arrow_down` / `content_paste`; **Blank** and **Load .txt / .srt** stay words.
- Subtitle style: caption box is shrink-to-fit (Align moves it relative to the Anchor point; may overflow the Stage) and only wraps at Stage width. News = white fill, regular weight, `ScaleY` 1.11, `Spacing` 1.68. Black outline is a **behind** `-webkit-text-stroke` copy (fill on top); never stroke and fill on the same span (OBS CEF has no `paint-order`; 8-way `text-shadow` is jagged on CJK). Show is larger, slightly gold, thicker behind-stroke. Font dropdown: **Web fonts (any computer)** vs **Installed on OBS PC**; Other… is a text field for a local family name (`customFontOpen`). The chosen font paints the whole cue, including English and digits. Latin runs use 0.4× 字距 on a CJK face (so DFHei tracking does not loosen English); a Latin face (Oswald, Bebas Neue, Inter, Segoe UI, Roboto, Impact, Arial) uses the full 字距. CJK default: 華康中黑體 / JhengHei. Style row: Bold / Italic / Underline / Strikethrough (icons) and Solid / Gradient. Gradient adds End color + Angle (default 90°, left to right); Start is the existing Text Color. Decoration and gradient are fill-only so the stroke copy stays a single color and the line is not drawn twice. Gradient clip is the literal class `.sub-fill.is-gradient` (`-webkit-background-clip: text`); OBS CEF drops the keyword `text` when it is passed through a CSS variable and paints a solid bar. Absent paint fields keep the old look. Overlay uses `vh`, not `cqh`; `document.fonts.load` before cue swap (400ms cap).
